Package: crossStatR
Type: Package
Title: Scientific Statistics for Biological, Electrochemical, Optical and Physics Experiments
Version: 0.99.3
Date: 2026-11-17
Authors@R: person("Rohan", "R", email = "phonics-tiffs1i@icloud.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
    comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0005-9225-1775"))
Author: Rohan R [aut, cre, cph]
Maintainer: Rohan R <phonics-tiffs1i@icloud.com>
Description: A unified scientific statistics framework for biological
    experiments, electrochemical measurements, optical and spectroscopic
    measurements, and experimental physics data. Combines established
    methods (descriptive statistics, hypothesis testing, regression, ANOVA,
    power analysis, mixed-effects variance decomposition, calibration,
    peak fitting) with diagnostic methods for experimental analysis
    (region-level signal difference testing, peak-evidence
    assessment, calibration-transfer risk, kinetic discrimination,
    experimental fragility, drift uncertainty attribution, analytical
    detection reliability, and stage-wise uncertainty-origin attribution).
    Every advanced method is documented with its mathematical formulation,
    assumptions, comparison with established alternatives, and known
    limitations. The package is intentionally conservative: it does not
    silently remove observations, does not select hypothesis tests solely
    on the basis of a normality-test p-value, and distinguishes technical
    from biological replicates in its variance models.
